# Task 4: Standard I/O Streams

## Objective

To demonstrate how a C program accepts user input and displays output using standard I/O functions.

## 1. C Source Code


#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    char name[50];

    printf("Enter your name: ");

    // Read string from standard input
    scanf("%s", name);

    printf("Hello, %s! Welcome to OS Class.\n", name);

    return 0;
}
```

## 2. Compilation

Compile the program:

```bash
gcc task4.c -o task4
```

## 3. Execution

Run the program:

```bash
./task4
```

Enter your name when prompted.

## 4. Expected Output

Example:

```text
Enter your name: Keshav
Hello, Keshav! Welcome to OS Class.
```

